==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 5.33~8.67 seconds<sup>160f~260f</sup>.
*4 [[Devil Wife|Devil Wives]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
*3 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Jumbo Jones]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Unlike the first stage, Jumbo Jones spawns on a timer. Like the first stage, however, this doesn't do much since you can still DPS down Jumbo Jones again. This stage tries to ruin this strategy with support from annoying enemies with Death Surges like Condemned Peng and a backliner to prevent easy chip damage in Sleipnir, but each Peng spawns infrequently and Sleipnir appears almost a minute into the stage, giving you ample time to kill Jumbo Jones.

At the start, clear the first Peng and Devil Wife before Jumbo Jones appears to prevent any  shenanigans with their Death Surges using units like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. Jumbo Jones will spawn and most likely unleash his Wave before the Peng dies, but the incoming Couriers you've spawned should be able to kill Condemend Peng. Once he's down, let Jumbo Jones kill your units and allow him to go near your base, where you'll do the exact same thing as the first stage: spam disposable DPS with Research combos until Jumbo Jones is dead. The exact same units as the first stage ([[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]) should be able to once again get enough damage to kill Jumbo Jones before he can unleash his attack, with assistance from Breakerblast and Sniper the Cat should your units be underlevelled. Once Jumbo Jones is dead, your stack should be able to walk up to Sleipnir and eliminate him from there, then go on to win the stage.

